    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the vulnerability. The crash confirms exactly the attack vector: `SEGV on unknown address 0x000041414141` at `internal_exr_validate_shared_attrs` validation.c:720, where the inline int32_t value `0x41414141` was dereferenced as a pointer by `memcmp`.\n\nThe PoC creates a multipart EXR file where both parts have an attribute named \"timecode\" but declared as type \"int\" instead of \"timecode\". When `internal_exr_validate_shared_attrs` compares shared attributes between parts, it looks up \"timecode\" by name, then dereferences `battr->timecode` as a pointer — but the union actually holds an inline `int32_t` value (0x41414141), causing a SEGV.",
